WEBVTT

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.930
<i>It's just before lights out,</i>
<i>there's a quietness,</i>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.730
<i>a stagnated mood,</i>

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.940
<i>and I'm responsible,</i>
<i>for half the reason, why it's like this.</i>

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.280
<i>But...</i>

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.700
<i>the original root of the problem</i>

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.070
<i>should be blamed on  the pilot,</i>
<i>El Hoshino, too.</i>

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.410
<i>Yeah, we were baffled,</i>
<i>here at Tsuiki, too.</i>

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:34.580
<i>Since Senior Master Sergeant Hoshino</i>
<i>had been assigned,</i>

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>the Tsuiki OTF has remained</i>
<i>in Foxtrot mode,</i>

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.250
<i>and we don't know the reason why.</i>

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.340
And it stayed in Hotel mode
for her predecessor, yes?

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.800
<i>Nonetheless, it can still take flight,</i>

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.180
<i>but we don't have a substitute pilot,</i>
<i>either.</i>

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.470
I understand. Thank you.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.520
So, the cause remains unknown?

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:58.230
If this persists,
it may hinder the next mission.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.900
But Vice-Minister Iiboshi
seems to have a plan in mind.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.740
Try to think of it this way.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.990
An OTF welcomes a pilot,
a foreign substance, into its body,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.870
and entrusts the pilot
to move it at will.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.500
There is no greater disgrace.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.250
Which is why... the OTF demand much
of their pilots.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.260
In exchange for relinquishing control
of their bodies,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.510
they hold onto their mental liberties.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:31.390
In other words,
the White Lover has a white heart,

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.310
a young maiden with a blank slate.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.350
That's where the aptitude test
came in, yes?

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:41.440
They are unsatisfied
because they believe they are incomplete.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.400
Precisely.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.900
By having the OTF by their sides

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.660
they have discovered their identities
for the first time.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.120
If there is a girl like that,

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.830
the OTF will allow the unification.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.540
But in El Hoshino's case,

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:00.420
her heart does not seem open to her OTF.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.000
You mustn't forget, Commander Sosoda.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.680
The one who chose her
was none other than the OTF, itself.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:16.930
DRAGON PILOT: Hisone &amp; Masotan

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.540
WHO LIKES TO BE DISLIKED

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.500
Yes!

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.460
ACM really is the best.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.800
Thanks to the OTF being grounded
for the time being,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.090
we can actually get back
to training for real.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.760
What's wrong with you?

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.180
You're not acting like you're
the leading male star.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:23.940
I feel like I really messed up, this time.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:28.650
-Oh, are you talking about El Hoshino?
-What're you getting worked up about?

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:33.450
This is when you wear her down
till she compromises, right? Fever time!

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.030
She's pretty worn down now.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.490
Now's the time. Now!

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.540
-Fever, fever!
-Hey, Castle!

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:41.750
-Fever, fever!
-Eel!

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.000
-Y-You think so?
-Oh yeah.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.880
Fever, fever!

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.010
We'll end here, for today.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.310
The briefing will commence at 1800.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.100
Until then,
you are all permitted free time.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.150
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:08.400
Dismissed.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.950
That chick is seriously in bad shape.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.160
Well, that's got nothing to do with me.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.670
Heave... ho!

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.670
You know, Futomomo,

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.880
I got angry.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.300
What should I do?

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:43.180
When a big girl like me gets mad,
it seems intimidating, doesn't it?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.060
They'll be afraid of me.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:08.750
Your pilot doesn't come to see you, huh?
Then how about if I ride you, instead?

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.800
Just kidding.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:18.800
What the hell.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.510
What should I do?

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.600
Everyone is mocking me.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.680
At this rate, we'll never be able
to meet halfway.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.850
Even hearing that aloud is jarring.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.520
I refuse to let anyone put me in my place.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:35.230
I wonder why
Hoshino won't acknowledge F-2.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.280
I'm the one not being acknowledged!

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.280
Embarrassed during a huge opportunity--

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:42.410
No, rather than embarrassment,
it was Hoshino's self-destruct--

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.950
-Eek! When did you--
-I should be asking you that!

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.080
U-Um...

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.580
I'm sorry!
I was muttering to myself again.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.760
Um... excuse me...

00:06:58.970 --> 00:06:59.800
What?

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:01.390
Stop following me.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.180
Even if you say that...

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.390
you're in front of my clothes...

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.650
Hoshino? Wait!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.190
I did it again.

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:17.780
Why do I always--

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.740
Huh?

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:23.240
This is...

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.540
What the hell. What the hell!

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:28.750
El!

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.920
Hello.

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:36.920
Um, well... what should I say?

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.420
Yesterday's training was rough--

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:45.890
Uh... well, I'm just saying,
nobody does well the first time...

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.970
So, uh... anyway,

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.140
you don't have to be so tight-breasted...

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:53.400
Ah! I just mean,
regardless if you're open or not,

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.480
-you know?
-Huh?

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.410
Zaito!

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:07.030
Are you back in fever mode? Fever!

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.240
Shut up!

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.250
Here are the details
about the training session.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.750
At 0500, tomorrow morning,

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:19.630
a live exercise will be held, offshore,
in the Japan Sea with your OTF.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.720
I thought the OTF were grounded.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:29.010
You will be observed on how you
and your OTF cope in a dire situation.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:33.560
The training's main purpose is to see how
you make decisions with limited resources,

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:36.480
and your teamwork, as Dragon Pilots.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:38.070
What the hell is that?

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:41.400
This training exercise
is extremely important.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.910
As a result, you may
be relieved of your Dragon Pilot duties.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.410
-What?
-Relieved of our Dragon Pilot duties?

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:50.200
I will explain the details the day of.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.160
As Dragon Pilots, be self-aware
and take on this challenge earnestly.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:55.500
That is all.

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:57.460
What should I do?

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.670
If I'm relieved of being a Dragon Pilot,

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.050
if Masotan is taken away from me,

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:05.970
I'll just be a misfit, with no sense
of personal space muttering to myself.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:08.890
With teamwork at the heart
of the training,

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:11.310
I'll never make it through this situation.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:14.810
Masotan?

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:16.810
He's trying to cheer you up.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.150
No!

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:26.490
I don't want to be apart from Masotan!

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:30.740
A-Amakasu!

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:34.450
I haven't given Masotan his bath yet...

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.210
Oh, Masotan!

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:39.920
You're all slimy
and taste like chlorine, Masotan!

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.510
I'm the same as El Hoshino.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:50.350
I never once thought of giving the OTF
a name or that it had feelings.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:54.430
But on that front,
you're very enlightened.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.690
That's why this big guy chose you.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:02.320
But Masotan has accepted you too, Kaizaki.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.820
-Huh?
-Don't worry.

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:08.740
You will all find a way
to work together, Amakasu.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.740
Like he said.

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:12.450
That's why you--

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:18.500
Nao, let me lick you, too!

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.920
Yuck! Dammit! Knock it off!

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:26.920
HISONE &amp; MASOTAN

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:46.150
Your training, this time, will take place
on that deserted island.

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:50.110
The training will be complete
once you've escaped the island

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:51.450
and returned to base.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:52.490
What?

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.410
Escape the island?

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.410
There are no boats
that will pass the coast,

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.420
and aircraft transit
has already been restricted.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:05.800
Therefore, there will be no one
to answer your distress calls.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.510
S-So does that mean

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.430
this is survival training?

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.260
What about using our OTF?

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:16.720
Of course,
returning via OTF is acceptable.

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.180
That is, if you can. However...

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:20.270
Huh?

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.230
...you only have one week.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.400
If you are unable to escape in that time,
we will be forced to retrieve you.

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:30.320
For this training, you have been supplied
with three days' worth of provisions.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:32.860
One, two, three, four...

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:34.530
That's four days short!

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:36.740
We'll be hungry.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.250
We might die.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.580
You must procure what you need
on your own, here.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:44.580
Keep in mind the main purpose is
to attempt to escape.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:45.790
That is all.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:59.060
What are you going to do, Hoshino?

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.690
I'm riding the OTF back to base.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:04.650
What about the survival part?

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:09.820
I'll get this training over with,
immediately.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.870
What's wrong?

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.370
Does your tummy hurt?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:23.040
I see. We're not supposed
to use ordinary methods.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.290
Why won't you fly?

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.550
What exactly... is going on?

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:35.510
At last, it has begun.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:38.810
This is for the day that will come?

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.220
Yes.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:44.640
For that purpose, they need to improve
their teamwork, and one more thing.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.810
They need to fulfill a condition.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.780
The emotions of those girls,
the White Lovers,

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:55.070
must be warmed up, by the OTF,
no matter what they are,

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.870
and incubate.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.040
Why won't they fly?

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.330
Is this island cursed?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:07.880
Oh my...

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:10.630
We have three days' worth of food.

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:13.130
In that time, we must find out why--

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:28.270
Oh, I didn't know dragons
ate people's food, too.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.940
Wait a minute!

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:33.190
W-W-What are we gonna do?

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.400
They won't retrieve us for a week!

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:38.280
He ate all the rare metal, too.

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:42.330
-How can it get any worse?
-Ah! Not the backpack!

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:45.580
I've got something precious in here!

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.010
What happened here?

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:02.180
Nao, why won't Masotan and the others fly?

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:05.680
"This ain't the time to be moping
about them not flying!"

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:08.020
Then, what should I do?

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:10.310
"Get your bearings together at first.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:13.280
Securing food and water should be
your first priority, dummy."

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:14.860
You're right!

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:17.900
We can't make strategy
on an empty stomach!

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.110
Got it!

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.490
Thanks, Nao!

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:26.910
What are you doing, Hitomi?

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.790
Dowsing.

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:30.460
D-Dowsing?

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.880
S-She's... crying.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:37.260
Futomomo ate everyone's food and water,

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:40.260
so the least I can do is search for water.

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:42.390
Yeah, I suppose so.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:46.600
Futomomo also ate all the rare metals.

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:49.980
We should look for rare metals together.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:54.860
If there were rare metals here,
it would cause a territory dispute.

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.820
Droves of suspicious boats would barge in.

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:00.820
But then again, maybe we'd be saved...

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.780
That's not to say,
you won't find rare metals!

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:05.870
Nao is rooting for you, too!

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.660
"You can do it, you can do it, Hitomi.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.790
You can do it, you can do it, Hitomi!''

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.250
On that note.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:26.180
Are you taking a siesta?

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:29.600
If they're coming in a week anyway,

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.270
then I will just breathe.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:32.650
No, no, no.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:35.770
Kinutsugai, did you forget
the main point of the training?

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:40.780
We were tasked with escaping the island
and returning to base, right?

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.530
Impossible...

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:46.280
Besides, we won't last a week
without water!

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.620
-It'll rain.
-Huh?

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.540
How do you know that?

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:53.540
I did... a rain dance.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.340
Rain dance?

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.180
As expected of you, Hoshino!

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:10.390
Escape by raft, right?

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:13.060
While it might not be much,
let me help you!

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:17.900
Oh, but we'd need a considerably
bigger raft to transport the OTF.

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:19.530
Aren't you being ridiculous?

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:22.780
There's no way we can make a raft

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:24.700
big enough to carry an OTF.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.990
So what do you plan on doing?

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.120
It's assumed we're supposed
to escape by air,

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:32.830
though, I don't know the reason
why the OTF can't fly anymore.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:36.040
S-So, all the more reason
to make a bigger raft.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:37.960
Weren't you listening?

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:42.090
We weren't ordered to return with our OTF.

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:55.100
<i>Leaving Masotan and the other OTF behind</i>
<i>while we escape is something I can't do.</i>

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:58.860
<i>Even if Hoshino is right...</i>

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:10.700
Now is when everyone's supposed
to work together.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.620
What's with this lack of solidarity?

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:16.540
Hey, say something, Nao.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.630
"What the hell are you talking about?

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:22.840
All you've done is make a fuss
and nothing else!"

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:24.970
You're right.

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:27.300
I haven't done anything.

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:30.100
Ah, I'm thirsty.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:31.770
Okay.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.520
Everybody!

00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.150
Technical Sergeant Amakasu will embark

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:47.780
on an excursion
to the north to find water.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.410
Who wants to join?

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.450
I see.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.620
No one is answering as usual.

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:59.080
Fine then. I'll go alone.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.970
Nothing, nothing. There's nothing here.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.440
I'm always spinning my wheels.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:29.070
Why are there torii gates here?

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:32.780
Is this the entrance to the underworld?

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:38.040
Is my life in this world
at an end, already?

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.920
I wasted my energy, screamed and shouted,

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:43.290
and yet now...

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:46.840
my dream to become a Dragon Pilot
will never come true!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:53.220
Masotan?

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.240
Masotan.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:13.200
What is this place?

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:17.870
Did you come looking for me
because you were worried?

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.880
Masotan!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.750
I love you!

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.140
Masotan, you don't taste salty.

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.180
You taste like delicious water.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:38.640
Everybody!

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:42.730
I've made the discovery of the century!
I found a spring in the back of a cave!

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:47.610
Ah, over here!

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:49.990
Who made the fire?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.110
Kinutsugai started it for us.

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:58.120
The key points for making a fire
are airflow creation and flammable tinder.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:01.710
Kinutsugai... for someone
who can't be bothered to do anything...

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:03.790
How rude.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.840
I think it's about ready.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:08.340
Oh my gosh, is that a yam?

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:11.050
Wild Japanese yam.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:13.050
Did you find it through dowsing?

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.090
Yes, in some capacity.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:16.390
Here. Eat up!

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:24.480
I have no right to eat that yam.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:30.440
I secretly held onto the hope
that everyone would fail

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:33.200
and that there was no one
more hard-working than me.

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:36.950
But in the end, everyone else
proved to be more useful.

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:38.910
I didn't do a thing.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.500
You know,

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:44.500
I always try to do my best,

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.880
but I end up burdening others.

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:49.710
I'm slow and dimwitted.

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:51.300
Despite that,

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:54.590
Futomomo still chose me.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:56.470
I was over the moon.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:01.310
That's why when Hoshino
spoke poorly of F-2,

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.810
it made me so angry.

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:05.980
I've never been so angry in my life.

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:10.730
I didn't like myself in the first place,
and now even more so.

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.740
It's the same with me.

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:18.780
I don't want to be separated from Akemi,

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:21.790
especially since I'm terrible
with human interaction.

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:24.790
Hitomi... Kinutsugai...

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:35.970
They look like they're having fun.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.050
Yeah.

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:41.100
Hey, maybe we don't need to rush
back to base.

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:42.020
What?

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:45.480
Let them play to their hearts,
and when they get hungry,

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:49.520
they'll say, "Let's go home!"
Maybe then, they will fly for us.

00:21:49.690 --> 00:21:50.520
Yeah!

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:53.480
We'll figure out something
for food and water,

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:56.780
and let Masotan and them
enjoy themselves for a week!

00:21:58.070 --> 00:21:59.320
I'm all for that.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.080
This is a good omen.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:05.290
The White Lovers have deepened their bond.

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:08.040
That can be attributed
to the existence of the OTF.

00:22:08.710 --> 00:22:13.050
It seems the OTF have also recalled
memories of one another.

00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:15.800
However, El Hoshino is still...

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:19.840
When she welcomes the OTF into her heart,

00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:23.180
a door will open to a new rule.

00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:31.560
I am not like you OTF zookeepers.

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:33.780
I am an F-2 pilot!

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:37.110
I'll prove that to you!

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:38.950
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:10.870
<i>The skin is...</i>

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:12.500
<i>Shouldn't you peel that?</i>

00:24:12.580 --> 00:24:14.710
<i>It was so hot on the outside.</i>

00:24:14.790 --> 00:24:18.090
<i>-I'll lick you!</i>
<i>-This chivalry and clumsiness.</i>

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:19.340
<i>Be one with him.</i>

00:24:19.420 --> 00:24:20.510
<i>Bang bang!</i>

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:22.630
<i>It's quite expected.</i>
